  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responding to urgent needs of internally displaced persons (IDPs) in Yemen with shelter and cash assistance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide shelter and non-food items and multi-purpose cash to internally displaced persons (IDPs) who do not wish to relocate. This IOM project provides transitional shelter, shelter rehabilitation support, and multipurpose cash assistance (MPCA) to help vulnerable people in the affected community to have access to improved living conditions and better able to meet basic needs as a result of this intervention. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 14,070 people, including 3,799 women, 4,080 men, 6,191 children, and including 310 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
